WEBVTT

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.050
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:06.210
Kei!

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.050
Minghua...

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.580
Did they hurt you?

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.660
Are you okay?

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.040
I heard they were going to interrogate you,
 and I got so worried.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.360
I'm fine. Nothing happened.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:21.480
I know it was a misunderstanding, 
but I'm still sorry we got rough with you.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.450
N-No, I'm sorry for making such a fuss.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.820
See you tomorrow, then.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.120
We'll be waiting.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:30.910
Right.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.800
<b>Komatsu Air Force Base</b>

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.390
I'm sorry.

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:47.590
For all that stuff I said.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:50.820
I was only thinking about myself.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.020
I wasn't thinking about 
how you felt, Minghua.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.570
No, I'm sorry.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.250
I think I went too far.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.750
Anyway, what was that about?

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.500
When he said, "See you tomorrow."

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.160
I'm going to be working part-time 
at the base starting tomorrow.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.460
Working?

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.470
It's late.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.820
Let's talk more tomorrow.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:50.460
You'll be rewarded for your cooperation.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.570
<b>Air Force Academy Handbook</b>

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.780
Come back tomorrow. Tell your friend 
you're working here part-time.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.140
<i>Help her fly...</i>

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:01.660
<i>Komatsu Rendezvous</i>

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:00.610
<i>I don't know what that means,</i>

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:05.250
<i>but if I can help defeat the Xi, 
I'll do whatever he wants me to.</i>

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.270
<i>A teenager in civilian clothes
 stands out pretty bad here.</i>

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.480
<i>But the inside of this base is pretty nice.</i>

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.400
<i>It's like a university campus.</i>

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:25.940
Hello.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:29.440
I came to get you.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.710
Where's Y-Yashirodoori?

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:32.730
Not here.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.080
Out.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.670
So I'll work with you today.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:38.780
Let's go.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.990
W-Wait!

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:53.300
You're the one who shot down the Xi 
off the coast of Shanghai, right?

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.260
Do you remember me?

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.840
Um... when you crashed...

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:05.580
No.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.010
I was so focused on what I was doing then

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:13.330
that I don't remember when I 
crashed or when I was recovered.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:14.560
Sorry.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.450
I s-see.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:19.630
I'm told you saved me.

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:20.830
Thanks.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.880
Tea and food. I'll go get them.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.020
Food?

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.930
I haven't eaten breakfast yet.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.740
The tea is for you.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.660
A secret weapon that eats?

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.160
I'm back.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:38.750
Where's my tea?

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:41.260
I'm back.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.860
Don't you need a spoon and some chopsticks?

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:46.680
I'm back.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:54.140
Listen, are you...

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:56.540
A scatterbrain?

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:57.870
I am not!

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:59.330
You are very wrong!

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:01.920
You don't seem like a weapon at all.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.150
You keep forgetting stuff, 
you talk kind of funny...

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.020
It's kind of like...

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:08.130
One more word and I'll get mad.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:23.540
I'm a little nervous.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:26.370
I've never talked to anyone from outside.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:27.630
Is that right?

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:33.260
So I'm just a little nervous.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:36.140
Narutani Kei.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:37.740
That's my name.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.710
We haven't introduced ourselves yet, right?

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:41.340
Kei?

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:43.870
So your name's Kei...

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:48.020
What should I call you?

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:49.590
Gripen.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:52.000
That's the name of an aircraft, right?

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.990
JAS39 Gripen.

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:57.360
That's who I am. Nothing else.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:01.280
Just as humans make no distinction between 
their brain and the rest of their body,

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:04.410
an Anima and a Daughter are 
identical and inseparable.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.590
I'm just a weapon.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:09.480
So call me Gripen.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:11.700
Got it. Gripen, right?

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:15.930
So, Gripen, what do we do after this?

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.780
What's next on the schedule after breakfast?

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.350
You don't have a plan?

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:24.490
What do you want to do, Kei?

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:26.340
I'm not sure how to answer that.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:30.370
Um... What is it that you usually do?

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:31.440
Here at the base.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.550
Walk.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.290
I wander around.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:38.540
Also, go on adventures here and there.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.490
You're a free-spirited weapon, huh?

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:42.660
Also, nap.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.650
Are you really that plane I saw?

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:00.370
What's with these people?

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:03.140
Oh, sorry.

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:04.980
That's H3.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.410
H3?

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:08.120
Hangar 3.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:11.290
The place you were held when 
you were abducted yesterday.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.290
Next to it is H2.

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.080
Next to that, H1.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.670
There are also smaller hangars:
H4, H5, and H6.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:20.320
This place is pretty big.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:25.200
This is the only base near the 
Sea of Japan that has any fighter jets.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:27.780
If the continental coast falls to the Xi,

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.790
Komatsu will be a front line base.

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:34.430
Taiwan and the peninsula are still fighting,
 so it's peaceful here now.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.010
But when they fall...

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:39.810
There's one runway.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:42.730
It's alternately referred to 
as Runway 06 and Runway 24,

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:45.020
depending on the direction 
of takeoff and landing.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.210
One runway?

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:49.900
But don't civilian planes land here?

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.630
They use it as well.

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.810
What if you need to do an emergency takeoff?

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:55.520
We share.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:58.840
What's this?

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:02.710
An old bunker. It's not used now.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.200
I like this place.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:10.770
I feel like a princess here.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.360
I see.

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:16.080
For an airplane, this is like a 
fancy bed with a canopy, huh?

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:17.020
Yes.

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:19.440
My secret base.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.600
But is that okay?

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.720
This is a JSDF base, right?

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:25.610
If you try to make it into your own room,

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.530
won't they get mad if they find out?

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:31.910
Haruka said that if you do something bad 
and nobody finds out, it's not bad.

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:33.040
Haruka?

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.830
Yashirodoori Haruka.

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:36.280
The director.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:39.350
Yeah, that sounds like something he'd say.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.950
Come sit.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.040
Sure.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:51.190
Fui ao jardim da Celeste, 
giroflé, giroflá.

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:57.090
Fui ao jardim da Celeste, 
giroflé, flé, flá.

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:59.150
What language is that?

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:00.520
I don't know.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:03.400
It was in the default training images.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:06.290
You were saying something off the 
coast of Shanghai too, right?

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:10.410
Um, Nova Elu... Nove Ere?

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:11.940
Nova Era.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:12.900
Yeah. That's right.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:15.900
I don't remember doing that,
 but I know what it means.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:18.610
"A new era."

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:21.590
Was that in your training images, too?

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:24.730
No, it was there from the start.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:25.840
The start?

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:28.380
I don't know where I learned it, but...

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:29.940
From the start.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.540
Yes? Roger.

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:41.260
I'm sorry. It's time for checkups.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.330
Checkups?

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:43.910
I need to go back.

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:46.140
I'll walk you to the gate.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:47.740
See you tomorrow.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:55.780
<i>Is she really that plane?</i>

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:59.540
Hey, Kei, do you have plans tomorrow?

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:02.360
Yeah, I've got my job at the base.

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:04.280
Two days in a row?

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.100
Well, fine.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.110
I'm going to Kanazawa.

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:09.220
Kanazawa?

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:13.070
I passed the review for 
my refugee application.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:16.570
I was hoping you could come with 
me if you were free, but...

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:17.790
Sorry.

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:21.430
Your grandparents are leaving 
tomorrow morning, too.

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:24.110
Don't bring any girls home!

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.640
I won't!

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:48.300
Coming, coming, coming, coming!

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:50.130
Hello, who's there?

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:53.040
Gripen?

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.370
Hello, Kei.

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:57.080
What are you doing here?

00:10:55.380 --> 00:11:06.390
<b>Narutani</b>

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:59.430
Someone from TRDI brought me here.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:00.500
TRDI?

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.320
The Technical Research 
and Development Institute.

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:06.390
So, um... why are you here?

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:12.740
Haruka told me to do whatever 
you told me to do.

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:14.060
Whatever I told you to do?

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.400
He said to let you have your way with me.

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:20.120
Don't resist, no matter what you do.

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:24.030
You're a young man, and some 
things are understandable.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:23.310
Let's have some fun!

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:26.000
Oh no!

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.610
Don't resist?

00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:29.250
Kids these days.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:31.210
Kei?

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.660
Just get inside!

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:43.460
Barley tea's fine, right?

00:11:46.690 --> 00:11:48.050
Is that you?

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:49.450
Yeah.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:56.600
This is a photo of me and my mom 
when we went flying in China.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:58.250
I think I was about ten?

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:00.690
She let me take over a little.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:03.110
You flew?

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:04.230
Through the sky? Yourself?

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:08.700
I've got over a hundred hours 
of flight time, you know.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:09.800
Wow.

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.330
Wow?

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:13.830
You've flown a lot more than me, right?

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:15.190
No...

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:18.460
I can't fly.

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:20.380
You can't?

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:22.560
During tests and during combat,

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:26.140
I always lose control in the middle of 
the flight and am sent back to base.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.080
I'm useless. Defective.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:30.400
They don't know why?

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:35.260
They keep giving me exams 
and finding nothing.

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:35.990
But...

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.350
But?

00:12:37.350 --> 00:12:41.190
It feels to me like I'm missing something.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:42.360
Like what?

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:43.500
I don't know.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:45.980
But that's how it feels.

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:48.870
How do you fly, Kei?

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:50.730
What can I do to fly right?

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:53.370
Um...

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:54.690
Well, let me think.

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:57.420
When I flew with my mom, she told me that

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:00.380
planes are built to fly, so if 
I was worried about what to do,

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:03.260
I should just do whatever came to mind.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:04.420
Without worrying about it?

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:08.160
Once you start thinking 
about it, you freeze up.

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:11.880
First, try to fly. Enjoy doing 
whatever you want to try.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:13.530
Maybe that's what she meant.

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.610
Then if I fly with your mom, 
maybe I'll get better.

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:23.290
If she can fly with me and help me,
 like she did with you,

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:25.440
I can feel safer when I'm in the air.

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:27.270
Can you ask her?

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:29.480
No.

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:30.940
Why?

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:32.740
My mom's gone.

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:39.140
She was doing stunts at an airshow when 
her plane was shot down by the Xi.

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:44.360
N-No, it's nothing you need to worry about.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:48.210
Though I guess I'd be lying if 
I said I was totally over it.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:52.940
So, um... I'm counting on you!

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:56.970
Get better soon and beat those Xi!

00:13:56.970 --> 00:13:59.160
So <i>we</i> can fly again.

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:01.520
So I can avenge my mom!

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:04.040
Okay. I'll do my best.

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:07.390
So... what am I doing my best at?

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:11.880
What is this?

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:15.660
When you're in trouble,
 you ask for divine help, I guess.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:20.630
<b>Uhashi Shrine</b>

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:17.510
Divine help?

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:20.630
Yeah. You pray you'll be able to fly better.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.820
I pray I'll be able to fly better.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.070
You don't need to actually say it.

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:30.140
What did you pray for?

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:33.170
That the Xi will be gone soon.

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:36.410
You don't like the Xi, Kei?

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:37.890
Of course not.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:41.600
You were made to fight them, weren't you?

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:43.410
Yes, but...

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:46.890
I've lost so many things because of them.

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:48.940
If it weren't for them...

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:52.790
I'll never forgive the Xi.

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:59.490
I pray that the Xi will be gone soon.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:03.750
You've never really left the base, right?

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.630
Yes.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.450
This is all new to me.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:10.230
At times like these,
if you just take it easy,

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:12.120
everything will sometimes just work out.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.090
I see.

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:14.290
That's good to know.

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:17.200
Oh, right. What do you want for lunch?

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:18.560
The daily lunch B set!

00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:21.460
It comes with one more 
side dish than the A set.

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:23.700
And a deep-fried dish, too, so it's better.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:26.450
Is that the meal at the JSDF cafeteria?

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:27.030
Yes.

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:29.760
Sorry, but there is no B set in this city!

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:32.150
What about the C set?

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:33.740
No C set, either!

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.280
My dreams are crushed.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:37.650
Don't worry.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.290
I'll give you something even better.

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:43.670
Here you go!

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:53.490
Let's eat.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.390
Okay, let's dig in.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:56.510
Okay.

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:10.070
It's good.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:11.310
I'm glad.

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:23.710
You've got soup on your face.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:26.460
What's this?

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:27.660
Gyoza.

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:29.390
Dip it in the sauce before you eat it.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:34.830
Hot!

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:37.710
You're not supposed to eat it so fast.

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:42.820
But it's good!

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:58.130
You two are close, huh?

00:16:58.130 --> 00:16:59.180
Your sister?

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:00.610
Yes, I guess.

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:03.090
Kei is my teacher.

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:06.260
He teaches me lots of things 
about the outside world.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:08.880
That's a good brother to have, huh?

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:14.210
<i>As the Chinese civil war escalates, 
what should Japan's response be?</i>

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.890
<i>Well, I think it's important 
to understand just what</i>

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:18.850
<i>it is these militants called the Xi want,</i>

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:22.410
<i>and be prepared to sit 
down and talk with them.</i>

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:22.410
<i>Sit down and talk with the Xi?</i>

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:25.350
<i>Is all Japanese media like this?</i>

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.240
The Xi, was it?

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:31.720
The weekly magazines talk about them
like they're some kind of alien invaders.

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:34.360
I wonder if they're going to attack Komatsu.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:35.650
Don't worry.

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:38.780
If they do, I'll protect the city.

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:42.460
Welcome!

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:45.760
Keep your mouth shut, dummy.

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:48.000
But it's important.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:52.010
I was made to protect humanity.

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:54.560
Even if I'm unstable during flight,

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:58.040
I need to fight until the very end
 and shoot down the enemy.

00:17:58.380 --> 00:17:59.770
<i>I see.</i>

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:03.960
<i>She's trying her best to protect humanity,
 in her own way.</i>

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:06.000
Kei...

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:08.710
I want more gyoza.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:25.410
The Gripen is an extremely unstable weapon.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:30.010
The slightest thing causes it to lose 
function and go out of control.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:33.420
My bosses are telling me they 
don't want to waste any more money

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:36.170
on a prototype without obvious potential.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:41.670
<i>But as a scientist, I want to keep 
struggling until the very end.</i>

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:44.900
<i>Will you help me?</i>

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:48.540
<i>Help her fly again.</i>

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:55.700
Here.

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:58.990
I didn't know what you liked...

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:00.860
So I just bought something at random.

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:03.200
If you don't like it, you can have this one.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:06.020
No, yogurt drinks are a favorite.

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:09.560
But I remembered something 
slightly unpleasant.

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:10.550
Unpleasant?

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:15.870
Someone once told me that my body 
wasn't developing properly,

00:19:15.870 --> 00:19:18.740
and I should drink lots of dairy products.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:21.790
If I liked sweets, 
then I should drink yogurt.

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:23.880
It would make my breasts bigger.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.410
It was very rude.

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:28.110
Y-Yeah.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:32.130
It's good.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:33.860
Oh, I'm glad you like it.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:37.680
This may be the first time 
I've ever drank yogurt.

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:39.120
What?

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:40.670
I thought you said it was a favorite.

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:44.740
Hey, Gripen!

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:46.200
What's wrong?

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.470
Are you okay?

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:48.970
Don't worry.

00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:50.770
She's asleep, that's all.

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.050
Yashirodoori...

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:54.300
"Yashirodoori-san" to you, Prince Charming.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.740
I'm older than you, you know.

00:19:57.290 --> 00:19:58.790
What are you doing?

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:01.460
Don't worry. They work for me.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.350
What is the point of all this?

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:11.570
Just leaving the two of us 
together with no explanation...

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:13.460
Three hours.

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:16.940
That's how often Gripen 
is awake, on average.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:20.080
That's usually how long it 
takes before she passes out...

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:23.350
Regardless of whether she's 
in the middle of the air or not.

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:25.770
But today...

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:30.640
That's right. She was up and 
about for over ten hours.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.380
I'm surprised.

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:36.410
And all she did was go on a 
child's idea of a date with you.

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:38.030
You were watching?

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:41.010
We have no idea what it 
is that wakes her up.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:45.830
I'd like to develop a hypothesis and 
investigate, but we don't have a lot of time.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:49.320
The date of her test 
flight has been decided.

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:50.870
Her test flight?

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:53.970
Exactly one week from today.

00:20:53.970 --> 00:20:55.710
If she can't fly right then,

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:57.220
she'll be scrapped this time.

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:58.510
Scrapped?

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:01.300
I did everything I could.

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:06.560
Well, just take it as a sign that 
Anima cost a lot more than you think.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:10.220
There's no denying the fact 
that they're inefficient.

00:21:10.220 --> 00:21:14.650
But the other Anima keep adding to 
their flight hours with no problems.

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:20.640
It makes sense to just scrap a plane with 
no future and move on to the next one.

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:21.660
But...

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:26.360
If it weren't for her, we'd be dead.

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:29.260
Then it's time pay her back.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:34.010
Stop whining and help us, Prince Charming.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:38.690
I've been wondering... 
Why do you keep calling me that?

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:42.480
Because in the fairy tales,

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:45.400
it's always Prince Charming's 
kiss that wakes up the princess.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:51.080
Even if it's the princess 
who goes in for the kiss first.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.290
Next time on <i>Girly Air Force</i>...

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:33.510
ALT 03: "Anima Core."

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:40.010
<i>Anima Core</i>

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:37.320
Barbie 01, cleared for take off!
